# UST.G3EG: H02 Component-12 Adaptive Exactness Cutset Theorem

**Status:** exact reduction closed; characteristic-zero promotion open
**Coefficient field:** \(K=\mathbb Q(\gamma)\), with
\[
\gamma^6+24\gamma^5+89\gamma^4+44\gamma^3+33\gamma^2+16\gamma+64=0.
\]

## 1. Scope

UST.G3EB reduced component-12 promotion to the exact nullity of a
\(42706\times2113\) quotient-retaining presentation. UST.G3EG makes that
object computationally tractable and audits three exactness routes. It proves
the reductions below, but it does not yet prove that the remaining ten finite
kernel directions exist over \(K\).

## 2. Exact kernel-preserving contractions

Four classes of pivots are performed symbolically over the integral
power-basis representation of \(K\):

| pivot class | count |
|---|---:|
| quotient-unit eliminations | 227 |
| paired \(t_1/t_2\) common-\(v\) eliminations | 254 |
| monic \(w^2-F_6\) eliminations | 676 |
| remaining literal \(\pm1\) pivots | 85 |
| **total** | **1,242** |

Every pivot coefficient is a unit in the coefficient ring used by the
presentation. Each row/column contraction is therefore an invertible
elementary elimination and preserves the kernel dimension over \(K\).

The first 1,157 pivots reduce the matrix to \(1324\times956\). The remaining
85 reduce it to

\[
M_{12}^{\rm sat}\in K^{1239\times871}.
\]

At \((21817,\gamma-5)\), these matrices have ranks 946 and 861 respectively,
so both retain finite nullity ten. The finite rank is evidence for the target;
the exact elementary equivalence is the theorem proved here.

## 3. High-precision split-algebra audit

All six Hensel lifts of the six roots of the defining polynomial modulo 21817
were carried to exponent 96, a modulus of 1,384 bits. For every embedding, the
\(1324\times956\) reduced matrix has rank 946 and a ten-vector kernel with
literal zero residual modulo the lifted prime power.

This rules out a single-root accident to that precision. It remains a local
\(p\)-adic statement and is not, by itself, a characteristic-zero kernel
certificate.

Unit-normalized rational reconstruction at exponents 64 and 96 stabilizes
exactly 600 coefficients: 590 prescribed zeros and ten prescribed units. No
nontrivial coefficient stabilizes. Thus direct coordinatewise reconstruction
in that normalization is not a viable proof route at the current precision;
the basis is determinant-sized.

## 4. Exact replay of six-embedding lattice candidates

The six embeddings must be combined before interpolation back to the power
basis of \(K\). An adaptive lattice calculation does this and then evaluates
every candidate literally in the exact \(1324\times956\) matrix. Its four
audited rounds give:

| samples | lattice dimension | coefficients over 500 bits | exact nonzero residual slots |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 10 | 120 | 29,465 | 10,795 |
| 15 | 150 | 21,344 | 9,378 |
| 20 | 180 | 13,619 | 7,507 |
| 25 | 210 | 1,843 | 3,279 |

The monotone reduction is useful evidence that the embeddings carry a common
algebraic object. The final residual is nevertheless nonzero. Accordingly no
candidate is accepted as an element of \(\ker_K M_{12}\), and component-12
rank 71 is not promoted.

A direct fraction-free route is also mathematically valid, but after 490 of
861 target pivots its coefficient height reached 104,650 bits. This records a
performance boundary, not a failed theorem.

## 5. Rank consequence and boundary

The proven global statement remains

\[
\boxed{4748\le\operatorname{rank}_K Q\le5112.}
\]

If ten independent exact kernel vectors are eventually replayed with zero
residual, component 12 will have rank 71 and the conditional interval will be
\(4748..5102\). Until then, neither conclusion may be asserted.

## 6. Reproducibility

Run the guarded aggregate and its independent finite-rank replay:

```text
python build_ust_g3eg_h02_component12_adaptive_exactness_cutset.py
python verify_ust_g3eg_h02_component12_adaptive_exactness_cutset.py
```

The packet is
`state/ust_g3eg_h02_component12_adaptive_exactness_cutset.packet.json`.
Exact reduction certificates are under `evidence/ust_g3ec/` and
`evidence/ust_g3ed/`; the six-embedding audit is under `evidence/ust_g3ef/`.

## 7. Remaining frontier

There are now two legitimate exits:

1. run the next 30-sample, 240-dimensional six-embedding stage using a
